Cell[TextData[{
 "Which is the best procedure to extract a secret key out of this raw \
distribution?\nThere is no answer in full generality, but we can notice a few \
things and propose a protocol which is a reasonable candidate for optimality. \
A good cryptography protocol should \n\t(i) present high correlations between \
Alice and Bob \n\t(ii)reduce Eve's information as much as possible. \nNow, in \
the raw data, we see that Alice and Bob are highly anticorrelated when x=y=1. \
It is thus natural to devise a procedure\nthat allows them to transform these \
anticorrelations in correlations. A good procedure reveals as little as \
possible information on the public channel.\nThe protocol proposal is the \
CHSH protocol:\n\t1 Distribution. Alice and Bob repeat the measurement \
procedure on arbitrarily many instances and collect their data.\n\t2 \
Parameter estimation. By revealing publicly some of their results, they \
estimate the parameters of their distribution, in particular \tthe fraction \
pNL of intrinsically nonlocal correlations.\n\t3 Pseudosifting. For each \
instance, Alice reveals x=0 or x=1, but not Bob. If (x=1,y=1)",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "\[DirectedEdge]"],ExpressionUUID->"5c895cb3-431e-4cc3-8def-f65804b4fa5e"],
 "(a,\[Not]b);\n\t4 Classical processing. The details depend on whether one \
considers "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
  3.9600090313343496`*^9, 
  3.9600091332625046`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1e54c99f-735f-4867-98b9-\
436ace589cae"],

Cell["\<\
\t\t1. one-way postprocessing \"error correction and privacy amplification,\" \
efficient in terms of secret key rate;\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
  3.9600090313343496`*^9, 
  3.9600091772741165`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"409b3f9e-e5a1-492a-b396-\
05715f8c344f"],

Cell["\<\
\t\t2. two-way postprocessing \"advantage distillation,\" inefficient for \
small errors but tolerating larger errors.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
  3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021166397425*^9, 
  3.9600211664383583`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e5eb77dc-ecd8-49e8-96c4-\
8cb7a9809f21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One-way post-processing:\n\nThe Devetak\[Dash]Winter bound for this setting \
is:\n\nr = H(A|E) - H(A|B)=I(A:B) - I(A:E) = H(A) - H(A|B)- I(A:E) =1 - \
H(A|B)- I(A:E)\n\nwith I(A:B) = H(A) - H(A|B) and since A \[Element]{0,1} is \
a fair bit (unbiased by design), H(A) = 1. Bob applies a random bit flip with \
probability q, independently of everything else. This alters the error rate \
between Alice and Bob. Let:",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"e", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["e", "AB"], "=", 
     RowBox[{"p", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a", "\[NotEqual]", "b"}], "|", "x"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e915f1ea-81f6-4c02-854b-ec1ed0aacc5f"],
 ": error rate before preprocessing. Then, after preprocessing: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["e", "'"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "-", "q"}], ")"}], "e"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"q", "(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", "e"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"e", "(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        RowBox[{"2", "q"}]}], ")"}], "+", "q"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"f360b871-8050-4fb5-b03b-0add1383c456"],
 ". This is just flipping Bob\[CloseCurlyQuote]s bit with probability q, \
which changes agreement a = b to disagreement a\[NotEqual] b, and vice versa. \
So the new error probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", "'"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f545de7d-a0ee-44f3-a5d2-0cd93ff6aece"],
 ", and: H(A|B) = h(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", "'"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9723e0fc-54ef-42ab-bbc1-d80ad4f746b6"],
 ") \[Implies]  = 1 - h(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", "'"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "374641f9-f91f-447d-977e-6c43d4e2f4e1"],
 "). We extract the key only from those settings after pseudosifting.\n\n\n\
After depolarization, Eve\[CloseCurlyQuote]s strategy is: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["p", "E"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["p", "L"], 
      StyleBox["1",
       FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
       FontWeight->"Bold",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        SubscriptBox["p", "L"]}], ")"}], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p",
        FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
        FontWeight->"Bold",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "NL"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "be6ee934-578d-4cfc-8212-9728185a9d41"],
 "\n* The local part: Eve knows a, and in half the cases she knows b. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "75bba18d-2e35-4525-a72c-e8be683440d1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["b", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "060b4f65-af0b-4d68-ac93-d7ff3143b206"],
 " are uncorrelated \[RightArrow] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"e", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"p", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a", "\[NotEqual]", "b"}], "|", "x"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5ad2c889-fc10-45ff-992f-783610bab2a6"],
 ".\n* The nonlocal part gives her no information at all.  Alice and Bob get \
perfect anticorrelation (which becomes correlation after pseudosifting) \
\[RightArrow] a=b after pseudosifting \[RightArrow]e=0. So the total is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"e", "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dac8ee2b-3431-4c2a-8de7-b88062e433ce"],
 ". From the table,"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.9600230868215504`*^9}, {3.960023126671065*^9, 3.9600231350691414`*^9}, 
   3.960023189844224*^9, {3.9600268308903875`*^9, 3.9600268693887787`*^9}, {
   3.960039790619465*^9, 3.9600398298329396`*^9}, {3.960039860634636*^9, 
   3.9600399022559867`*^9}, {3.960039937886054*^9, 3.960040051406867*^9}, {
   3.960040146496413*^9, 3.960040146496413*^9}, {3.960040980996419*^9, 
   3.9600409837201004`*^9}, {3.9600874565205092`*^9, 
   3.9600874569181423`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2a975ccb-8edd-49b9-85e6-\
0f8689eb1cc8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     RowBox[{"ab", "\\", "e"}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"?", ",?)"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", 
       RowBox[{"?", ")"}]}]}], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", "b"}], ")"}]},
    {"00", 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "2"], 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "8"], 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "4"]},
    {"01", "0", 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "8"], "0"},
    {"10", "0", 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "8"], "0"},
    {"11", 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "2"], 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "8"], 
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "4"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}]],
  ExpressionUUID->"4501a4f0-2871-4ceb-8c4e-d22ecca98054"],
 "e=p(a\[NotEqual]b|x=y=1)=1-p(a=b|x=y=1). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.9600230868215504`*^9}, {3.960023126671065*^9, 3.9600231350691414`*^9}, 
   3.960023189844224*^9, {3.9600268308903875`*^9, 3.9600268693887787`*^9}, {
   3.960039790619465*^9, 3.9600398298329396`*^9}, {3.960039860634636*^9, 
   3.9600399022559867`*^9}, {3.960039937886054*^9, 3.960040051406867*^9}, {
   3.960040192716999*^9, 3.960040452521163*^9}, {3.960040544772949*^9, 
   3.960040680927903*^9}, {3.960040726108039*^9, 3.9600409778443236`*^9}, {
   3.960087464700071*^9, 3.9600874714461956`*^9}, {3.960540579920575*^9, 
   3.9605405800118027`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ea49202-d82c-4ccc-9201-\
fb232b52d79b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "From ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p",
     FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
     FontWeight->"Bold",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "NL"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9c526483-b5df-4321-adf5-4922142da88f"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"p", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ab", "|", "x"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["p",
          FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
          FontWeight->"Bold",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], "NL"], "(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ab", "|", "x"}], "=", 
         RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
      FractionBox[
       SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "4"]}], "=", 
     TagBox[GridBox[{
        {"\[Piecewise]", GridBox[{
           {
            RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "+", 
             FractionBox[
              SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "4"]}], 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["p",
                FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], "NL"], "(", 
              RowBox[{"a", "=", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"b", "|", "x"}], "=", 
                RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}]}], ")"}], "=", "1"}]},
           {
            FractionBox[
             SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "4"], 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["p",
                FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], "NL"], "(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"a", "\[NotEqual]", "b"}], "|", "x"}], "=", 
               RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}], "=", "0"}]}
          },
          AllowedDimensions->{2, Automatic},
          Editable->True,
          
          GridBoxAlignment->{
           "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, 
            "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
          
          GridBoxItemSize->{
           "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, 
            "Rows" -> {{1.}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
          GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
              Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
               Offset[0.84]}, 
              Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {
              Offset[0.2], {
               Offset[0.4]}, 
              Offset[0.2]}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
          Selectable->True]}
       },
       GridBoxAlignment->{
        "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}},
          "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
       GridBoxItemSize->{
        "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{1.}}, 
         "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
            Offset[0.35]}, 
           Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {
           Offset[0.2], {
            Offset[0.4]}, 
           Offset[0.2]}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}}],
      "Piecewise",
      DeleteWithContents->True,
      Editable->False,
      SelectWithContents->True,
      Selectable->False,
      StripWrapperBoxes->True]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d556d25c-4f76-436f-a8c5-cf77c47ac1eb"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.9600230868215504`*^9}, {3.960023126671065*^9, 3.9600231350691414`*^9}, 
   3.960023189844224*^9, {3.9600268308903875`*^9, 3.9600268693887787`*^9}, {
   3.960039790619465*^9, 3.9600398298329396`*^9}, {3.960039860634636*^9, 
   3.9600399022559867`*^9}, {3.960039937886054*^9, 3.960040051406867*^9}, {
   3.960040192716999*^9, 3.960040452521163*^9}, {3.960040544772949*^9, 
   3.960040680927903*^9}, {3.960040726108039*^9, 3.9600409778443236`*^9}, {
   3.960087464700071*^9, 3.9600874714461956`*^9}, {3.9605405858056574`*^9, 
   3.9605405858217316`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e680c77a-8cb9-44e6-bc32-\
ef1784f2759b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "From ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["1",
      FontFamily->"Times New Roman",
      FontWeight->"Bold",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "L"], ":", " ", 
    TagBox[GridBox[{
       {"\[Piecewise]", GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox["p", "L"], 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
            FractionBox["1", "2"]}], "\[Placeholder]"},
          {
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "(", 
             RowBox[{"a", "\[NotEqual]", "b"}], ")"}], "=", 
            FractionBox["1", "2"]}], "\[Placeholder]"}
         },
         AllowedDimensions->{2, Automatic},
         Editable->True,
         GridBoxAlignment->{
          "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, 
           "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
         GridBoxItemSize->{
          "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, 
           "Rows" -> {{1.}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
             Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
              Offset[0.84]}, 
             Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {
             Offset[0.2], {
              Offset[0.4]}, 
             Offset[0.2]}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
         Selectable->True]}
      },
      GridBoxAlignment->{
       "Columns" -> {{Left}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}, 
        "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
      GridBoxItemSize->{
       "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {{1.}}, 
        "RowsIndexed" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
           Offset[0.35]}, 
          Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "ColumnsIndexed" -> {}, "Rows" -> {
          Offset[0.2], {
           Offset[0.4]}, 
          Offset[0.2]}, "RowsIndexed" -> {}}],
     "Piecewise",
     DeleteWithContents->True,
     Editable->False,
     SelectWithContents->True,
     Selectable->False,
     StripWrapperBoxes->True]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "81959924-69ba-4fe8-9b80-3d255b5387b2"],
 "because each (a,b) pair has probability 1/4, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"e", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"p", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a", "\[NotEqual]", "b"}], "|", "x"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{"y", "=", "1"}]}], ")"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "\[CenterDot]", 
        FractionBox["1", "2"], "\[CenterDot]", 
        FractionBox["1", "2"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "\[CenterDot]", "0"}]}], "=", 
      FractionBox[
       SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "4"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "adb9d3d2-a069-4f43-92ac-a16a9fdca911"],
 ".\nLet's recall the table in the main text:\n* In half of the local \
strategies (4 out of 8), Eve knows both a, b,\n* In the other half, Eve knows \
only a, and has no knowledge of b.\nAfter Bob's random flip, her prior \
knowledge of b is only useful when she knows b and the flip does not occur. \
Her effective knowledge of a remains unchanged:\n* With probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "/", "2"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4a334226-e238-48b7-970a-97f9ecb98a05"],
 ", she knows b, but the flip introduces a bit-noise h(q),\n* In the \
remaining cases, she either doesn't know b or it comes from the nonlocal part \
(which gives no info).\nSo:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.9600230868215504`*^9}, {3.960023126671065*^9, 3.9600231350691414`*^9}, 
   3.960023189844224*^9, {3.9600268308903875`*^9, 3.9600268693887787`*^9}, {
   3.960039790619465*^9, 3.9600398298329396`*^9}, {3.960039860634636*^9, 
   3.9600399022559867`*^9}, {3.960039937886054*^9, 3.960040051406867*^9}, {
   3.960040192716999*^9, 3.960040452521163*^9}, {3.960040544772949*^9, 
   3.960040680927903*^9}, {3.960040726108039*^9, 3.9600409778443236`*^9}, {
   3.960087464700071*^9, 
   3.9600874714461956`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b11052fb-7f2b-4a99-8dc5-\
c6a87908ee1b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\t\t\t\t\t", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"I", "(", 
         RowBox[{"A", ":", "E"}], ")"}], "=", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           FractionBox[
            SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "2"], 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             RowBox[{"h", "(", "q", ")"}]}], ")"}]}], "\[Implies]", 
          "                           ", "r"}], "=", 
         RowBox[{"1", "-", 
          RowBox[{"h", "(", 
           RowBox[{"e", "'"}], ")"}], "-", 
          RowBox[{
           FractionBox[
            SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "2"], 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             RowBox[{"h", "(", "q", ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
       "EquationNumbered",ExpressionUUID->
      "92f12437-8440-4330-b1a2-35e0a8dcbff1"], ",", "  ", 
     RowBox[{Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "=", 
         RowBox[{"1", "-", 
          SubscriptBox["p", "NL"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "EquationNumbered",
       ExpressionUUID->"bfb98683-3d8a-40a8-a008-847b4476c83b"], " ", "and", 
      " ", Cell[BoxData[
       FormBox[
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["p", "NL"], "=", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", "v"}], "-", "1"}], "=", 
          RowBox[{
           SqrtBox["2"], 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             RowBox[{"2", "D"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
       "EquationNumbered",ExpressionUUID->
       "7f79c554-3fc5-452c-9344-807bdf5e559a"]}]}], "EquationNumbered"]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "EquationNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.960023085785823*^9}, {3.9600231921330776`*^9, 3.9600232187850714`*^9}, 
   3.96002683550534*^9, {3.9600269633775015`*^9, 
   3.9600269649898567`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9b7391e4-6e64-4ba8-badf-\
3cd840e5fabe"],

Cell["\<\
Note that in the local part, Eve always knows Alice\[CloseCurlyQuote]s bit a \
\[LongDash] because:
* Eve chooses the local deterministic strategy,
* Alice announces her input x (as part of the pseudosifting procedure),
* Therefore, Eve can compute a = a(x), deterministically.
So, for the local part, one might naively think:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960023237204226*^9, 3.9600233392524433`*^9}, {
   3.9600268395229115`*^9, 3.9600268453110056`*^9}, 
   3.960026876252571*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f727c7da-5688-4f95-9a42-\
08a6fd7c0978"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\t\t\t\t\t", 
   StyleBox[Cell[BoxData[
     FormBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"I", "(", 
        RowBox[{"A", ":", "E"}], ")"}], "=", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "\[CenterDot]", "1"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "-", 
            SubscriptBox["p", "L"]}], ")"}], "\[CenterDot]", "0"}]}], "=", 
        SubscriptBox["p", "L"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "EquationNumbered",
     ExpressionUUID->"c6d0013d-55d1-4362-88e6-93346e206676"], 
    "EquationNumbered"]}], TraditionalForm]], "EquationNumbered",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96000897755957*^9, 3.960008977904088*^9}, {
   3.9600090313343496`*^9, 3.960009172032612*^9}, {3.960021168486585*^9, 
   3.9600214888508873`*^9}, {3.9600215387299123`*^9, 3.960021543445548*^9}, {
   3.9600215793387537`*^9, 3.960021723179657*^9}, {3.9600227657871494`*^9, 
   3.960023085785823*^9}, {3.9600231921330776`*^9, 3.9600232187850714`*^9}, {
   3.9600234070697927`*^9, 3.9600234360674086`*^9}, 
   3.960026847849633*^9},ExpressionUUID->"920479e0-ca84-4137-96ef-\
8fd3c7e2993c"],

Cell["\<\
But this is not the relevant quantity in this protocol. Here's why: Although \
Eve knows a, the key is extracted from correlations between a and b. The \
protocol aims to produce identical bits a = b after pseudosifting and \
postprocessing. But since Eve never learns Bob's input y (it's not \
announced), and Bob may also apply random bit flips with probability q, Eve \
cannot be sure of what Bob's bit is\[LongDash]even if she knows a. So the bit \
ultimately held by Alice and Bob after postprocessing (which becomes the key \
bit) is not simply a. That's why the relevant mutual information is not \
I(A:E), but the effective information Eve has about the final key bit. That \
key bit is a, but Bob's processing makes it inaccessible without knowing his \
flip q and his private input y.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960023440809118*^9, 
  3.960023558357176*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"08dd1ee6-d92a-4506-94f0-\
b070d6c95b20"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the local part, Eve always knows a, and in half the local strategies, \
she also deterministically knows b. But she does not know whether Bob has \
flipped his bit b \[Rule] b+1 (mod 2), since that's randomized with \
probability q. So if Eve knows b, then her uncertainty on the postprocessed \
b' is h(q), and she still knows a. Thus, her information about the raw key \
bit a is 1, but her information about the final key bit (which requires that \
Alice and Bob agree) is reduced because the bit from Bob may have been \
flipped, and Bob's bit is needed to extract the key. Therefore the correct \
result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"I", "(", 
    RowBox[{"A", ":", "E"}], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox["p", "L"], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      RowBox[{"h", 
       RowBox[{"(", "q", ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "71caa628-0508-474a-b1f8-a7de2ea5f648"],
 ".\nThe formula ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"I", "(", 
     RowBox[{"A", ":", "E"}], ")"}], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["p", "L"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b7dc83e3-2d0f-413c-9ed7-67b84779c435"],
 " would only be valid if the raw key bit were taken as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["a", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b9cef054-e65e-4fd0-b9ed-c00f621a4332"],
 "  directly. But the key is derived from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "=", "b"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "59fea185-c462-4108-acbf-dc3688aeea9c"],
 " (after postprocessing), and since Eve doesn't control or learn Bob's side, \
the relevant mutual information is significantly lower. To avoid this \
confusion and better reflect the true dependency of the key on both Alice\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s and Bob\[CloseCurlyQuote]s outputs, and to clarify why \
Eve\[CloseCurlyQuote]s knowledge is limited, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s useful to \
reframe the mutual information not as I(A:E), but rather as the mutual \
information between the key bit and Eve\[CloseCurlyQuote]s knowledge. Let\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define the final key bit used in the protocol as K := A + \
B\[CloseCurlyQuote] (mod 2), where A is Alice\[CloseCurlyQuote]s output \
(publicly known to Eve), B\[CloseCurlyQuote] := B + 1 (mod 2) with \
probability q is Bob\[CloseCurlyQuote]s (possibly flipped) bit.  A=B\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]\[Implies]K=0. The goal is to make K = 0 as often as \
possible (i.e., correlated outputs), Eve\[CloseCurlyQuote]s information \
should be about K, not about A alone. Therefore I(K:E) = H(K) - H(K|E). If \
Eve can perfectly guess K, then H(K|E) = 0, so I(K:E) = H(K);  If Eve is \
completely ignorant of K, then H(K|E) = H(K), so I(K:E) = 0. Since Eve doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t know Bob\[CloseCurlyQuote]s flip q, nor his input y, her \
knowledge about the key bit K is not maximal, even if she knows A perfectly.\n\
\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960023440809118*^9, 3.96002363395444*^9}, {
  3.960026183739733*^9, 3.960026352181464*^9}, {3.960026631234683*^9, 
  3.9600266704672375`*^9}, {3.9600271457207603`*^9, 3.96002722315609*^9}, {
  3.9600272650475054`*^9, 3.9600272981346393`*^9}, {3.960027378922939*^9, 
  3.9600274922279944`*^9}, {3.960027540510845*^9, 
  3.960027679224863*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c9efb48c-e643-491d-85f7-\
8151de067732"],

